open-bt-rig-interface — licensing overview

Copyright (c) 2026 Reid Crowe, N0RC

This repository is source-available. It contains hardware designs, firmware,
a host-device protocol, tools and documentation, each under its own license.
The full license texts are in the LICENSES/ directory, and per-file licensing
follows the REUSE specification (SPDX headers and REUSE.toml).

  Path                                          License                          Commercial use
  hardware/ (KiCad designs, enclosure CAD)      CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0                  commercial license required
  firmware/                                     PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0     commercial license required
  protocol/ (spec + golden vectors), tools/,    MIT                              allowed
    CI files
  documentation (docs/, *.md)                   CC-BY-4.0                        allowed

Commercial use of the hardware or firmware (for example selling boards, kits
or assembled units, or putting the design or firmware in a product) requires
a separate commercial license from the copyright holder. See COMMERCIAL.md.

Third-party components keep their own licenses and are not covered by the
non-commercial or commercial terms above. Their required notices are in
THIRD_PARTY.md.

Where a file carries its own SPDX-License-Identifier, that identifier governs
the file.

Licensing history: before this change (up to and including commit b4041a4 on
the dev branch), hardware/ was licensed CERN-OHL-P-2.0 and firmware/ was
licensed MIT. Copies obtained under those earlier terms remain under them; all
later versions are licensed as described above.
